			"contents": "Volume 1, Chronicle 2\nThe Mesh Bag\n\n\"To whomever finding my son, please,\nI beg you, keep him save.\nand raise him into a good man.\nHis name is Arthur, and I am sorry:\nhis lastname is a secret I must refrain from telling you.\nBegins the voice in the Halo.\nWhen Arthur shall come to me one day and \ntell me who his foster parents were\nI'll repay you with more water and batteries than you'd need for a lifetime\"\nPromised, the Voice.\n\"And when he has grown into a strong body and\nlearned a critical mind, please pass him this Halo.\"\nArt stares at the glowing torus, as the light spins slowly\nas if it is loading its memory.\n\"Arthur. when you are listening to this, that means\nyou have survived, and fallen into good hands.\nFor that alone I am grateful. \nAnd I do not know how many years it would have taken\nfor you to become strong and sharp,\nbut anything less, \nand given what I am about to ask you to do,\nwould equal to asking you to die.\"\nCold sweat flows down Art's neck\nas he listens to this voice for the first time\nwho is supposed to be his father,\ntalking about his death.\n\"Your mother is very special, arthur,\nand that makes you also unusual.\nSimply put, most who knew of your existence think you are dead,\nand its better that way.\nExcept,\"\nCame silence.\n\"You have a destiny. \nA mission.\"",
